{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running an automated cobbler/scaffold code generation pipeline (task ID 5504) to implement srd077-cksum requirements R3.2 and R3.3 in the go-unix-utils project. The task requires:\n   - R3.2: Ensure cksum exits 1 when any file cannot be opened or an invalid algorithm is specified\n   - R3.3: Ensure cksum handles SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n   - Modify `cmd/cksum/main.go` to add any missing functionality\n   - Modify `cmd/cksum/cksum_test.go` to add differential test cases for R3.2 and R3.3\n   - Pass acceptance criteria: `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test` must all succeed\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: Go binary vs GNU reference binary (gcksum) comparison via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - CRC-32 POSIX checksum computation\n   - Algorithm selection (sha1, sha224, sha256, sha384, sha512, blake2b, sm3)\n   - Tagged vs untagged output formats for non-CRC algorithms\n   - Raw binary digest output mode\n   - `pkg/hashutil` for non-CRC hash operations\n   - Exit code conventions: 0 for success, 1 for errors\n   - stderr normalization in tests via `discardStderr` for error message differences between Go and GNU implementations\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd077-cksum.yaml`\n     - Contains the full SRD specification. R3.2: \"Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened or an invalid algorithm is specified.\" R3.3: \"Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\"\n     - Non-goals: No --check mode for CRC verification, no --base64 encoding.\n\n   - `cmd/cksum/main.go` (existing, 241 lin