d R3.3\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Add differential test case(s) for R3.2 (invalid algorithm producing exit 1) to `cmd/cksum/cksum_test.go`\n   - Verify existing R3.2 code coverage in `cmd/cksum/main.go` is complete (it appears to be)\n   - Verify existing R3.3 coverage is complete (it appears to be)\n   - Run `go build ./cmd/cksum/`, `go vet ./cmd/cksum/`, and `go test ./cmd/cksum/ -count=1` to verify acceptance criteria\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three required files (SRD spec, main.go, test file) and was about to plan and implement the changes. The analysis shows:\n   - The code in `cmd/cksum/main.go` already handles both R3.2 and R3.3 functionally\n   - The test file needs at least one new differential test case for R3.2's \"invalid algorithm\" error path (exit code 1). The \"file cannot be opened\" path is already tested via \"missing-file\" and \"missing-among-valid\" test cases.\n   - R3.3's TestSIGPIPE already exists and tests the SIGPIPE handler\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Add a differential test case for invalid algorithm to `cmd/cksum/cksum_test.go`, specifically:\n   - A test with `--algorithm=invalid` that expects `ExitCode: 1` with `discardStderr` normalizer (since error message format may differ between Go and GNU implementations)\n   - Potentially add a comment referencing R3.2 and R3.3 to existing test cases\n   - Then run `go build -o bin/cksum ./cmd/cksum/`, `go vet ./cmd/cksum/`, and `go test ./cmd/cksum/ -count=1` to verify all acceptance criteria pass\n\n   The task description states: \"Implement srd077-cksum requirement R3.2 per the specification\" and \"Implement srd077-cksum requirement R3.3 per the specification\" with acceptance criteria requiring build, vet, and test to pass.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or 